## Magic mount timing: post-fs-data
source: https://topjohnwu.github.io/Magisk/details.html
### post-fs-data

This triggers on `post-fs-data` when `/data` is decrypted and mounted. The daemon `magiskd` is launched, Safe Mode is evaluated (if the device failed to reach `boot-complete` twice in a row, or if Safe Mode was triggered via key combo or the Magisk app, all modules and Zygisk are disabled), `post-fs-data` scripts and module `system.prop` files are processed, and enabled module files are magic mounted.


## AOSP init boot order: post-fs-data before zygote-start
source: platform_system_core/rootdir/init.rc android16-release
1:on late-init
2:    trigger early-fs
8:    trigger fs
9:    trigger post-fs
16:    trigger late-fs
20:    trigger post-fs-data
23:    trigger load-bpf-programs
24:    trigger bpf-progs-loaded
27:    trigger zygote-start

